# Interactive boots skip the finite integration-test sysinit scenario.
# BusyBox init keeps both services alive until the machine is powered off.
::respawn:/bin/httpd -f -p 8080 -h /
::respawn:/bin/sh -i
# GitHub issue #862: SIGQUIT to PID 1 makes BusyBox init exec this in place
# of itself, so PID 1 runs a new image and then exits (the fail-stop line).
# Inert until something sends pid 1 SIGQUIT; only the PTY smoke does.
::restart:/etc/restart.sh
